    "field": "Paleoclimatology",
    "problem": "The link between atmospheric CO2 and climate during the Eocene greenhouse remains uncertain because geological CO2 records are fragmented and have low temporal resolution, which is insufficient to test modeling suggestions that warmer climates are more sensitive to CO2 forcing than colder ones.",
    "method": "This study proposes a method to test for state-dependent climate sensitivity by combining a new high-resolution CO2 record from boron isotopes in foraminifera with novel Global Mean Temperature estimates to reconstruct Equilibrium Climate Sensitivity (ECS) through the Eocene.",
    "task": "The task is to test the hypothesis of state-dependent climate sensitivity during the Eocene by combining new high-resolution, proxy-based CO\u2082 records with temperature estimates to determine if warmer climates were more sensitive to CO\u2082 forcing than colder ones.",
